Brief notes on the key decisions before the JSON:

- **`versionNumber: "1.2.0.NEXT"`** — the `.NEXT` build placeholder makes the Dev Hub assign the next build number automatically.
- **`ancestorId: "HIGHEST"`** — resolved by the Dev Hub at build time to the highest *promoted/released* version of the package, so no one ever has to edit the file after a release. (The promoted versions' `04t` aliases aren't needed for this.)
- **`buildNumberIncrement: "Auto"`** — build number increments on every `sf package version create`.
- **`apexTestAccess`** — assigns the packaged permission set and the `SalesConsoleUser` permission set license to the user running Apex tests during package version creation (the fixture metadata/class are never packaged because `triage-test-fixtures` has no `package` key).
- **`triage-test-fixtures`** — listed as a package directory (so `sf project deploy start` targets it in scratch orgs), not default, and belonging to no package, so it can never be included in the managed package or installed in subscriber orgs.

